* s01_ng.lib -- ngspice version of 2-pump-characterization/client-board-models.lib (generated by hand, P2)
* Discrete cards (MJD340, MJD350, BAS16, DI_BZX84C5V1) copied unchanged from lines 1-166.
* OPAGEN: 3-compliance-and-limiter/tools/generator/ngspice_core.lib (limit() rewritten as min(max())).
* INA149G / TLE2141G: copied unchanged. TI VSWITCH macromodels left out (not used by S01/S02).

* =====================================================================
* client-board-models.lib  --  all models for the STIM (bootstrapped Howland) stage
* One .include covers the whole schematic.  Rev A, 2026-10-16.
*
*  Part (board ref)        Model name       Source                               Edits made here
*  MJD340  (Q2, top NPN)   MJD340           Diodes Inc. PSpice, 21JUL2010        '=' added to NE/RB/RE; QUASIMOD removed
*  MJD350  (Q1, bot PNP)   MJD350           Diodes Inc. PSpice, 21JUL2010        QUASIMOD removed
*  BAS16LT1G (D1, D2)      BAS16            Fairchild/onsemi, Rev 0.0 2009       none
*  5V zener  (D3, D4)      DI_BZX84C5V1     Diodes Inc. (PLACEHOLDER until the   none  (subckt: pins A K)
*                                           board's zener marking is read)
*  INA149  (U2)            INA149           TI sbomc47 v1.1, 03/03/2022          VCCVS1_IN given explicit 0 V value
*  TLE2141 (U1)            TLE2141          TI slom459a Final 1.1, 12FEB2019     none
*
*  >>> The schematic uses INA149G and TLE2141G (bottom of this file): LTspice-robust
*  >>> equivalents. LTspice could not solve this circuit with TI's VSWITCH-based models.
*
* Why QUASIMOD is removed: it made LTspice's .op fail ("Singular matrix
* q1#quasi"). Quasi-saturation needs VCE < Ic*RCO (~0.3 V); Q1/Q2 never get
* there in this circuit, so nothing physical is lost.
* Checked in ngspice 42 (see README): hFE, VBE, Vf, Iq vs datasheet ballpark.
* =====================================================================

